# id|label|repo|ref|description. repo is a git URL or path relative to project root starting with '/'.
# ref is a git tag or branch, or "-" for the default branch; ignored for local directories.
# Each source must have install.sh at its root. Ids must be unique across desktops.list.

# DEs
gnome|GNOME|/gnome|-|Modern, polished, Wayland-first desktop
xfce|Xfce|/xfce|-|Lightweight traditional desktop
kde|KDE Plasma|/kde|-|Highly configurable, feature-rich desktop
lxqt|LXQt|/lxqt|-|Very lightweight desktop, good for old hardware
cosmic|Cosmic|/cosmic|-|Modern Gnome-Inspired desktop (Unofficial Trixie build)
mate|MATE|/mate|-|Lightweight GNOME 2 successor
cinnamon|Cinnamon|/cinnamon|-|Traditional desktop with Windows-style layout

## WMs
openbox|Openbox|/openbox|-|Minimal stacking window manager
i3|i3|/i3|-|Tiling window manager for X11
labwc|labwc|/labwc|-|Wayland window manager with floating windows, inspired by Openbox
sway|Sway|/sway|-|Tiling window manager for Wayland inspired by i3
hyprland|Hyprland|/hyprland|-|Highly-customizable tiling compositor for Wayland (Backported)
